  "title": "Seneca Falls Convention",
  "summary": "On 19–20 July 1848 about 300 people met at the Wesleyan Chapel in Seneca Falls, New York, for a women's rights convention planned by five women. The Declaration of Sentiments, listing 16 grievances, was read on each day and signed by 100 attendees. GovInfo says the convention laid the foundation for the Nineteenth Amendment, which granted women the vote in 1920.",
